## What I learned
- Selector types: type (`h2`), universal (`*`), class (`.price`),
  ID (`#footer`), grouping (`h1, h2`), chaining (`.card.recommended`),
  descendant (`#footer .desc`)
- **One space changes everything:**
  - `.a.b`  = one element that has BOTH classes ("one body")
  - `.a .b` = element `.b` INSIDE element `.a` ("parent and child")
- `#hero.dark` = chaining works with id + class too
- "syntax" means: the rule of HOW to write something
- If the same property is declared twice, the later rule wins (= cascade, next lesson)
- Absolute links must start with the protocol: `https://` —
  without it the browser treats it as a relative path (404)
- Finally typed this from memory after 4 fails:
  `<a href="https://google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">`
  - target = where to open, `_blank` = new tab
  - rel = relationship, two values in ONE pair of quotes
  - no+opener (block access), no+referrer (hide origin, r×3)

